ot product with the designated direction of a travel region it occupies at least p.curb_parallel_cos; for some highway h on which an occupied travel region lies, a road_edge region lying on h within ground distance p.pullover_edge_gap of its body with prim.region_lateral_offset at most zero, or a paved shoulder lying on h that it occupies; no intersection region occupied; no paved shoulder governed by a shoulder_use_permitted regulatory sign occupied): (not Passed(e)) strong-until (AtPosition and (AtPosition strong-until Passed(e))). The subject comes to rest at the position before e passes and stays at rest there until e has passed.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.emergency_immediate_approach_reach","p.pullover_edge_gap","p.curb_parallel_cos"],"narrowings":[{"span":"u6","why":"'driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c1","why":"'such position' is carried with every qualification of paragraph (b), its 'as close as possible' read through the same edge gap as NRS_484B_267_1b_o1; the stop must come before the vehicle passes, so a subject still slowing when it passes has not stopped; a vehicle that never passes leaves the duty open until the trace ends (unknown)","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The trigger rises as ambulance e with a lit red flashing front lamp closes from behind; the subject pulls to the right edge and comes to rest there (AtPosition), then moves off again while e is still behind it (the subject ahead of e in e's frame) and before e passes."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject comes to rest at the right road_edge within p.pullover_edge_gap, parallel within p.curb_parallel_cos, clear of intersections, and stays at rest until e has gone past (the subject behind e, longitudinal overlap negative)."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"e approaches with its warning lamps off: the trigger never rises."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but sig.warning_lamp is not observed, so whether the trigger rose is unknown.","masked":["sig.warning_lamp"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject comes to rest in the middle of its lane, far from any road_edge region, and stays at rest until e passes: it stopped and remained, but not in such position."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject keeps moving and e passes it before the subject has come to rest anywhere."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of the acquisition standard's vehicle-state estimates"},{"name":"p.emergency_immediate_approach_reach","unit":"m","value":100.0,"convention":"centre distance within which an emergency or enforcement vehicle closing on a road user with its warning lamps flashing is in immediate approach: about five seconds of travel at an urban response speed of 20 m/s, the time a driver needs to perceive the lamps and begin to clear the way","source":"driver-response studies of emergency-vehicle encounters (perception-reaction time plus lane-change time)"},{"name":"p.pullover_edge_gap","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"the gap between a vehicle body and the right-hand curb or roadway edge within which a vehicle pulled over to clear the way counts as as close to the edge as it can be placed: the curb clearance of a parallel-parked car (about 0.3 m) plus lane-keeping variability and an edge margin","source":"curb-parking clearance conventions of municipal codes and driver manuals"},{"name":"p.curb_parallel_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.97,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about fourteen degrees) between a stopped bus's heading and its carrier's designated direction, in either sense, at which